":"td","children":["-\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Reroll one damage roll per encounter.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sigil Crystal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sigil_Crystal","referenceId":"reference:8e34a2be0886d98c"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Traditional Jewels"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Traditional_Jewels"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Varies\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force"}," bonus on damage rolls.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Solari Crystal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Solari_Crystal","referenceId":"reference:a6ac3efe1a2966df"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Traditional Jewels"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Traditional_Jewels"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Varies\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force"}," bonus to ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Deflect"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Deflect"}]}," attempts.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Synthetic Crystal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Synthetic_Crystal","referenceId":"reference:5a4dbd43d68a3c53"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Synthetic Crystals"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Synthetic_Crystals"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Red or Varies\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+1 bonus on attack rolls.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Unstable Crystal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unstable_Crystal","referenceId":"reference:6cd73214ac0f3b56"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Synthetic Crystals"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Synthetic_Crystals"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Red or Varies\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+1 die of damage on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Critical Hits"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Critical_Hits"},"; deactivates on a Natural 1.\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Creating New Lightsaber Crystals"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["There are other types of Lightsaber Crystals besides the ones covered above, but their effects are identical to the Lightsaber Crystals detailed above. Beyond those, these is the potential to have entirely new Lightsaber Crystals that have yet to be discovered and used in Lightsabers. Creating unique Lightsaber Crystals that can be used in the creation of a Lightsaber can be a good way to reward ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," heroes, who typically are less interested in the acclimation of credits and other wealth. A unique Lightsaber Crystal as a reward for completing a major story arc (or fulfilling one's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Destiny"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Destiny","referenceId":"reference:373d368333d789ee"},") can be a compelling motivator for a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," hero, and though most ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," eschew possessions, an enhancement to a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi's"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," weapon of choice is often worth undergoing a difficult quest, mirroring the Jedi Trials they face in the transition from apprenticeship to knighthood.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For Gamemasters looking to create a unique Lightsaber Crystal, first come up with an interesting story behind the crystal. Why is it renowned? Who possesses it now, and what are they doing with it? If possible, weave the story of the crystal into the larger tapestry of your campaign's storyline. Additionally, if you are designing an entire adventure around obtaining this Lightsaber Crystal, make sure to get the entire party involved; maybe the crystal is in the possession of your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," hero's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Crime Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Crime_Lord","referenceId":"reference:6f4563ed64c9640b"}," arch-nemesis, and getting it back means dealing with that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Crime Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Crime_Lord","referenceId":"reference:6f4563ed64c9640b"}," once and for all. Maybe the crystal was stolen from the family of the party's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"},", and retrieving it is a point of honor. Whatever the story behind the Lightsaber Crystal, do not hesitate to make sure that it is of interest to the entire party and not just the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," character in the group.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Once you are satisfied that the crystal has a suitable history, you can decide what effect(s) to grant the wielder of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," with that Lightsaber Crystal. A unique Lightsaber Crystal can be slightly more powerful than the Lightsaber Crystals presented above, though not much more so. In general, a unique Lightsaber Crystal should confer a bonus about on-par with most standard crystals' bonuses, or maybe a little more powerful. Any bonuses the weapons confers should be typed as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force"}," bonuses, and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill"}," bonuses and damage bonuses should be around +2 for unconditional bonuses, or around +5 for highly conditional bonuses.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Accessories and Modifications"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A Lightsaber is more than just a hilt and blade. Some Jedi like to customize their Lightsabers to best fit their needs. Most Jedi choose simple, functional Accessories and Modifications that enhance their fighting styles, and as such Modifications such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blade Locks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blade_Locks"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pressure Grips"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pressure_Grips"}," are common.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["At the time a Lightsaber is created, the crafter can choose one of the following Lightsaber Accessories or Modifications to apply to their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," at no additional cost in time or credits. A character with the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tech Specialist"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tech_Specialist","referenceId":"reference:62e86e4173a4731b"}," feat can add one additional Lightsaber Accessory or Modification, which counts toward the weapon's one-modification limit.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["EFFECT\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Beckon Call"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beckon_Call","referenceId":"reference:55292594e1d23a3a"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Can summon a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," using a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Slave Circuit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Slave_Circuit"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Blade Lock"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blade_Lock","referenceId":"reference:e23274a4a9eb6410"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Locks the blade on, so it doesn't accidentally deactivate when ",{"tag":"a","children":["Thrown"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Thrown"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Concealed Compartment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concealed_Compartment","referenceId":"reference:530c45be3a79d481"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["A secret compartment that can store a Fine-sized object.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Electrum Detail"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Electrum_Detail","referenceId":"reference:c92a1b5d260e2008"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["A symbol of rank and skill, similar to a badge or honor.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Fiber Cord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fiber_Cord","referenceId":"reference:9f7d62a8e6157b1c"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["A cord is tied to the end of a Lightsaber, making the wielder harder to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disarm"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disarm","referenceId":"reference:0449aa195af99b14"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force-Activated"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force-Activated","referenceId":"reference:421acb5c0d2192be"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Lightsaber can only be activated through the use of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Interlocking Hilt"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Interlocking_Hilt","referenceId":"reference:3306f1fee3c86317"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["A hook attached to the end of single-bladed Lightsaber, allowing it to attach to another Lightsaber with this Accessory.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Pressure Grip"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pressure_Grip","referenceId":"reference:68dbeb380ba45c44"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Lightsaber automatically disables itself when not being held.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Trapped Grip"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trapped_Grip","referenceId":"reference:f834dd27862dd112"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Booby-traps the Lightsaber with a hidden mechanism, can be deactivated with a hidden knob or button.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Waterproof Casing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Waterproof_Casing","referenceId":"reference:5e4f1bf8f9ecac93"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Lightsaber can function normally while underwater.\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
